# Line endings: LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the WORKING TREE too, not just the blobs. That half matters on
# Windows, where `core.autocrlf=true` would otherwise check source files out as
# CRLF: any tool that rewrites one with LF endings then leaves that file looking
# modified while `git diff` shows nothing at all. Several generators in this repo
# can produce exactly that, and it is a genuinely confusing state to debug.
#
# `text=auto` leaves git's own binary detection in charge, so committed binary
# assets are unaffected by the rule above.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-braces for the binary asset types committed here: never normalize,
# never diff as text, whatever the heuristics decide. Add to this list when a new
# kind of binary asset lands. (Not .svg — that one is XML, and normalizing it is
# both correct and what you want.)
*.webp binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
